da-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` (line 142)\n3. Kernel: `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` at `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (line 157)\n   - **Grid dimensions**: `(num_row_blocks, trace_width)`\n   - **Block size**: Powers of 2, related to skip_domain\n\n**MLE Rounds 1..=n_stack**\n1. `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` (line 794) - Called once per MLE round\n2. **Critical per-AIR/per-trace loop** (line 833-901):\n   - Iterates over `self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)` - **each window represents one AIR**\n   - For each window (AIR), determines branching:\n\n     **Path A: Degenerate case** (line 848-878)\n     - Condition: `log_height < l_skip + round` (typically for n < 0 cases)\n     - Calls: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate()` at `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` (line 245)\n     - **THIS IS THE BOTTLENECK**: Only 1 kernel launch per AIR\n     \n     **Path B: General case** (line 880-901)\n     - Condition: `log_height >= l_skip + round`\n     - Calls: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round()` at `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` (line 209)\n     - Auto-tuned grid with multiple blocks\n\n### **Kernel Details**\n\n**`stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_kernel`** (CUDA: line 228)\n- **Parameters**:\n  - `q_evals`: Array of pointers to evaluation matrices (per commit_idx)\n  - `eq_r_ns`, `k_rot_ns`: Segmented EQ evaluations\n  - `unstacked_cols`: Array of `UnstackedSlice` structures (one per column)\n  - `lambda_pows`: Batching coefficients\n  - `output`: u64 atomic accumulator array `[S_DEG * 4]`\n  - `q_height`: Matrix height\n  - `window_len`: Number of columns in this window/AIR\n  - `num_y`: `1 << hypercube_dim` = number of parallel evaluations\n- **Grid**: \n  - `grid.x = kernel_launch_params(num_y, 256).x` (based on num_y)\n  - `grid.y = tuned_stride` (auto-tuned: typically 4-16)\n- **Shared Memory**: `ceil(blo