ugh GPU contention might limit the gains. Another approach is pre-sorting AIRs by height and using a 2D grid where different heights are processed in parallel.\n\nThe real win though is fusing constraint and interaction evaluation in Round 0 — that's where the biggest regression happened, jumping from 178ms to 662ms. Since the AIRs are already sorted by height, I can batch the constraint evaluation across same-height AIRs in a single kernel launch instead of launching separately for each one.\n\nLet me check the current implementation to see if this approach is actually viable.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9387,"cache_read_input_tokens":69472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9387},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fb0c9c1-c32f-45e4-afe7-f108d55d0327","uuid":"e80a68ad-b911-4c8d-940f-e2736eaf607e"}
