{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0191yNq1HE8wwgj229atos5k","type":"tool_result","content":"595\t    // PERF[jpw]: we could return evals and batch zerocheck poly by degree before interpolating.\n596\t    // Cannot do it for logup because we need to calculate the sum claims.\n597\t    #[instrument(name = \"prover.rap_constraints.ple_round0\", level = \"info\", skip_all)]\n598\t    fn sumcheck_uni_round0_polys(\n599\t        &mut self,\n600\t        ctx: &ProvingContext<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n601\t        lambda: EF,\n602\t    ) -> Result<Vec<UnivariatePoly<EF>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n603\t        self.mem\n604\t            .emit_metrics_with_label(\"prover.batch_constraints.before_round0\");\n605\t        self.mem.reset_peak();\n606\t        let n_logup = self.n_logup;\n607\t        let l_skip = self.l_skip;\n608\t        let xi = &self.xi;\n609\t        let h_lambda_pows = lambda.powers().take(self.max_num_constraints).collect_vec();\n610\t        self.lambda_pows = Some(if !h_lambda_pows.is_empty() {\n611\t            h_lambda_pows.to_device()?\n612\t        } else {\n613\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n614\t        });\n615\t        // Precompute lambda combinations for all AIRs with monomials\n616\t        let lambda_pows_ref = self.lambda_pows.as_ref().unwrap();\n617\t        for (air_idx, air_pk) in self.pk.per_air.iter().enumerate() {\n618\t            if air_pk.other_data.zerocheck_monomials.is_some() {\n619\t                self.lambda_combinations[air_idx] = Some(\n620\t                    compute_lambda_combinations(self.pk, air_idx, lambda_pows_ref)\n621\t                        .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::LambdaCombinations)?,\n622\t                );\n623\t            }\n624\t        }\n625\t        let num_present_airs = ctx.per_trace.len();\n626\t        debug_assert_eq!(num_present_airs, self.n_per_trace.len());\n627\t\n628\t        self.eq_3b_per_trace = ctx\n629\t            .per_trace\n630\t            .iter()\n631\t            .enumerate()\n632\t            .map(|(trace_idx, (air_idx, _))| {\n633\t                let vk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx].vk;\n634\t                let num_interactions = vk.num_interactions();\n635\t                if num_interactions > 0 {\n636\t                    let n = self.n_per_trace[trace_idx];\n637\t                    let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n638\t                    let mut b_vec = vec![F::ZERO; n_logup - n_lift];\n639\t                    let mut weights = Vec::with_capacity(num_interactions);\n640\t                    for interaction_idx in 0..num_interactions {\n641\t                        let stacked_idx = self\n642\t                            .interactions_layout\n643\t                            .get(trace_idx, interaction_idx)\n644\t                            .unwrap()\n645\t                            .row_idx;\n646\t                        let mut b_int = stacked_idx >> (l_skip + n_lift);\n647\t                        for bit in &mut b_vec {\n648\t                            *bit = F::from_bool(b_int & 1 == 1);\n649\t                            b_int >>= 1;\n650\t                        }\n651\t                        let weight =\n652\t                            eval_eq_mle(&self.xi[l_skip + n_lift..l_skip + n_logup], &b_vec);\n653\t                        weights.push(weight);\n654\t                    }\n655\t                    weights\n656\t                } else {\n657\t                    vec![]\n658\t                }\n659\t            })\n660\t            .collect_vec();\n661\t        self.d_eq_3b_per_trace = self\n662\t            .eq_3b_per_trace\n663\t            .iter()\n664\t            .map(|eq_3bs| {\n665\t                if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n666\t                    Ok(DeviceBuffer::new())\n667\t                } else {\n668\t                    eq_3bs.to_device()\n669\t                }\n670\t            })\n671\t            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;\n672\t\n673\t        // Precompute logup combinations for all traces with interaction monomials\n674\t        for (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in ctx.per_trace.iter().enumerate() {\n675\t            let air_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n676\t            if air_pk.other_data.interaction_monomials.is_some()\n677\t                && !self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx].is_empty()\n678\t            {\n679\t                self.logup_combinations[trace_idx] = Some(\n680\t                    compute_logup_combinations(\n681\t                        self.pk,\n682\t                        *air_idx,\n683\t                        &self.d_beta_pows,\n684\t                        &self.d_eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx],\n685\t                        &self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx],\n686\t                        &self.beta_pows,\n687\t                    )\n688\t                    .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::LogupCombinations)?,\n689\t                );\n690\t            }\n691\t        }\n692\t\n693\t        // PERF[jpw]: we could also build the layers for different n in a transposed way using\n694\t        // eq_nonoverlapping_stage_ext, which is more memory efficient\n695\t        for &n in &self.n_per_trace {\n696\t            let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n697\t            if let Entry::Vacant(entry) = self.eq_xis.entry(n_lift) {\n698\t                let layers =\n699\t                    EqEvalLayers::new_rev(n_lift, xi[l_skip..l_skip + n_lift].iter().rev())\n700\t                        .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::EqEvalLayers)?;\n701\t                entry.insert(layers);\n702\t            }\n703\t        }\n704\t\n705\t        self.sels_per_trace_base = self\n706\t            .n_per_trace\n707\t            .iter()\n708\t            .map(|&n| {\n709\t                let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n710\t                let height = 1 << n_lift;\n711\t                let mut cols = F::zero_vec(3 * height);\n712\t                cols[height..2 * height - 1].fill(F::ONE); // is_transition\n713\t                cols[0] = F::ONE; // is_first\n714\t                cols[2 * height + height - 1] = F::ONE; // is_last\n715\t                let d_cols = cols.to_device()?;\n716\t                Ok(DeviceMatrix::new(Arc::new(d_cols), height, 3))\n717\t            })\n718\t            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, MemCopyError>>()?;\n719\t\n720\t        let selectors_base = self.sels_per_trace_base.clone();\n721\t\n722\t        // All (numer, denom) pairs per present AIR for logup, followed by 1 zerocheck poly per\n723\t        // present AIR\n724\t        let mut batch_sp_poly = vec![UnivariatePoly::new(vec![]); 3 * num_present_airs];\n725\t        let d_lambda_pows = self\n726\t            .lambda_pows\n727\t            .as_ref()\n728\t            .expect(\"lambda powers must be set before round-0 evaluation\");\n729\t\n730\t        // Loop through one AIR at a time; it is more efficient to do everything for one AIR\n731\t        // together\n732\t        for (trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, selectors_cube, public_values, eq_3bs)) in izip!(\n733\t            &ctx.per_trace,\n734\t            &self.n_per_trace,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fb0c9c1-c32f-45e4-afe7-f108d55d0327","uuid":"974839d0-e8a2-4968-bbe7-b366cae1f45a","timestamp":"2026-04-12T19:29:10.418Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs","content":"    // PERF[jpw]: we could return evals and batch zerocheck poly by degree before interpolating.\n    // Cannot do it for logup because we need to calculate the sum claims.\n    #[instrument(name = \"prover.rap_constraints.ple_round0\", level = \"info\", skip_all)]\n    fn sumcheck_uni_round0_polys(\n        &mut self,\n        ctx: &ProvingContext<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n        lambda: EF,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<UnivariatePoly<EF>>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n        self.mem\n            .emit_metrics_with_label(\"prover.batch_constraints.before_round0\");\n        self.mem.reset_peak();\n        let n_logup = self.n_logup;\n        let l_skip = self.l_skip;\n        let xi = &self.xi;\n        let h_lambda_pows = lambda.powers().take(self.max_num_constraints).collect_vec();\n        self.lambda_pows = Some(if !h_lambda_pows.is_empty() {\n            h_lambda_pows.to_device()?\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        });\n        // Precompute lambda combinations for all AIRs with monomials\n        let lambda_pows_ref = self.lambda_pows.as_ref().unwrap();\n        for (air_idx, air_pk) in self.pk.per_air.iter().enumerate() {\n            if air_pk.other_data.zerocheck_monomials.is_some() {\n                self.lambda_combinations[air_idx] = Some(\n                    compute_lambda_combinations(self.pk, air_idx, lambda_pows_ref)\n                        .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::LambdaCombinations)?,\n                );\n            }\n        }\n        let num_present_airs = ctx.per_trace.len();\n        debug_assert_eq!(num_present_airs, self.n_per_trace.len());\n\n        self.eq_3b_per_trace = ctx\n            .per_trace\n            .iter()\n            .enumerate()\n            .map(|(trace_idx, (air_idx, _))| {\n                let vk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx].vk;\n                let num_interactions = vk.num_interactions();\n                if num_interactions > 0 {\n                    let n = self.n_per_trace[trace_idx];\n                    let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n                    let mut b_vec = vec![F::ZERO; n_logup - n_lift];\n                    let mut weights = Vec::with_capacity(num_interactions);\n                    for interaction_idx in 0..num_interactions {\n                        let stacked_idx = self\n                            .interactions_layout\n                            .get(trace_idx, interaction_idx)\n                            .unwrap()\n                            .row_idx;\n                        let mut b_int = stacked_idx >> (l_skip + n_lift);\n                        for bit in &mut b_vec {\n                            *bit = F::from_bool(b_int & 1 == 1);\n                            b_int >>= 1;\n                        }\n                        let weight =\n                            eval_eq_mle(&self.xi[l_skip + n_lift..l_skip + n_logup], &b_vec);\n                        weights.push(weight);\n                    }\n                    weights\n                } else {\n                    vec![]\n                }\n            })\n            .collect_vec();\n        self.d_eq_3b_per_trace = self\n            .eq_3b_per_trace\n            .iter()\n            .map(|eq_3bs| {\n                if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n                    Ok(DeviceBuffer::new())\n                } else {\n                    eq_3bs.to_device()\n                }\n            })\n            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;\n\n        // Precompute logup combinations for all traces with interaction monomials\n        for (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in ctx.per_trace.iter().enumerate() {\n            let air_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n            if air_pk.other_data.interaction_monomials.is_some()\n                && !self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx].is_empty()\n            {\n                self.logup_combinations[trace_idx] = Some(\n                    compute_logup_combinations(\n                        self.pk,\n                        *air_idx,\n                        &self.d_beta_pows,\n                        &self.d_eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx],\n                        &self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx],\n                        &self.beta_pows,\n                    )\n                    .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::LogupCombinations)?,\n                );\n            }\n        }\n\n        // PERF[jpw]: we could also build the layers for different n in a transposed way using\n        // eq_nonoverlapping_stage_ext, which is more memory efficient\n        for &n in &self.n_per_trace {\n            let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n            if let Entry::Vacant(entry) = self.eq_xis.entry(n_lift) {\n                let layers =\n                    EqEvalLayers::new_rev(n_lift, xi[l_skip..l_skip + n_lift].iter().rev())\n                        .map_err(LogupZerocheckError::EqEvalLayers)?;\n                entry.insert(layers);\n            }\n        }\n\n        self.sels_per_trace_base = self\n            .n_per_trace\n            .iter()\n            .map(|&n| {\n                let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n                let height = 1 << n_lift;\n                let mut cols = F::zero_vec(3 * height);\n                cols[height..2 * height - 1].fill(F::ONE); // is_transition\n                cols[0] = F::ONE; // is_first\n                cols[2 * height + height - 1] = F::ONE; // is_last\n                let d_cols = cols.to_device()?;\n                Ok(DeviceMatrix::new(Arc::new(d_cols), height, 3))\n            })\n            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, MemCopyError>>()?;\n\n        let selectors_base = self.sels_per_trace_base.clone();\n\n        // All (numer, denom) pairs per present AIR for logup, followed by 1 zerocheck poly per\n        // present AIR\n        let mut batch_sp_poly = vec![UnivariatePoly::new(vec![]); 3 * num_present_airs];\n        let d_lambda_pows = self\n            .lambda_pows\n            .as_ref()\n            .expect(\"lambda powers must be set before round-0 evaluation\");\n\n        // Loop through one AIR at a time; it is more efficient to do everything for one AIR\n        // together\n        for (trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, selectors_cube, public_values, eq_3bs)) in izip!(\n            &ctx.per_trace,\n            &self.n_per_trace,","numLines":140,"startLine":595,"totalLines":1605}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ArdJD8XMPsTXriVmCFvJDh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a full picture. Let me write the detailed plan. The key changes:\n\n1. **Pre-compute interaction DAGs/rules for all AIRs** — Move the DAG construction from inside the loop to before the loop. This front-loads CPU work.\n\n2. **Pre-allocate per-AIR output buffers** — Instead of allocating output buffers inside `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`, pre-allocate them all before the loop.\n\n3. **Launch all kernels without D2H sync** — Remove the `to_host()` calls from inside the loop. \n\nInstead, keep the DeviceBuffers and sync+copy after all AIRs are processed.\n\n4. **Share intermediate/temp buffers** — Since kernels on `cudaStreamPerThread` execute serially, a single set of intermediate buffers (sized for the max across all AIRs) can be reused.\n\n5. **Batch D2H copy and post-processing** — After all kernel launches, sync once and process all results.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the concrete changes. The main loop in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` at `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884` is where I need to restructure the work.\n\nBefore the loop, I'll precompute metadata for each AIR: constraint degrees, coset counts, the interaction DAG with symbolic rules and weights, and GPU pointers to main parts. Then I'll scan across all AIRs to find the peak buffer sizes needed, allocate those shared buffers once, and set up per-AIR output storage.\n\nOnce everything's staged on the GPU, I'll launch both the zerocheck and logup kernels for each AIR back-to-back without waiting for results. After all kernels are queued, a single synchronization point lets me transfer the computed evaluations back to host memory and process them sequentially.\n\nTo make this efficient, I need to pre-compute the interaction rules and their associated GPU buffers ahead of time rather than rebuilding them for each AIR. I'm defining a data structure that captures the symbolic rules, encoded rules buffer, and weight buffers so they're ready to use when the kernels launch.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the memory implications of pre-allocating all these output buffers across 623 AIRs—each one needs space for numerator and denominator weights, and while individual AIRs are small, the aggregate could add up significantly depending on the domain sizes.\n\nThe intermediate scratch buffers are trickier since they vary per AIR, so I need to track the maximum size and reuse that single allocation across all kernel launches. This is actually more efficient than the current approach of allocating and freeing per-AIR, even accounting for CUDA's memory pooling behavior.\n\nSince kernels on the same stream execute sequentially, the scratch buffer is guaranteed to be free when the next kernel starts, but I need to be careful about how I pass it—as a raw pointer or slice rather than transferring ownership. For error handling, I should decide whether to fail fast on the first kernel launch error or collect all results and report them together.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2759,"cache_read_input_tokens":114399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2759},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fb0c9c1-c32f-45e4-afe7-f108d55d0327","uuid":"1226cead-fe27-42d8-a049-0032da872a4e"}
