{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EAnL5LkvUTmGpwxyv5HwQM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pipeline Round 0 Kernel Launches\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR GPU synchronization in the Round 0 constraint evaluation loop to allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back without CPU stalls. This targets the largest sub-component regression in \"STARK excl. trace\": Round 0 increases from 178ms (APC 0, 99 AIRs) to 662ms (APC 300, 623 AIRs) despite a >2x reduction in total cells and constraints.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\tThe bottleneck is in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884`.\n10\t\n11\t**Call chain (per AIR iteration, lines 732-880):**\n12\t1. CPU: Prepare per-AIR data (constraints DAG, trace pointers, etc.)\n13\t2. `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` at `round0.rs:31-124`:\n14\t   - Allocates `intermediates` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n15\t   - Allocates `temp_sums_buffer` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n16\t   - Allocates `sp_evals` output buffer\n17\t   - Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` kernel via FFI\n18\t   - Returns `sp_evals` DeviceBuffer (intermediates and temp_sums dropped = `cudaFreeAsync`)\n19\t3. **SYNC**: `sum_buffer.to_host()` at `mod.rs:792` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n20\t4. CPU: Transpose, iDFT, polynomial construction → `batch_sp_poly[2*N + trace_idx]`\n21\t5. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` at `round0.rs:132-275`:\n22\t   - **CPU**: Builds `SymbolicDagBuilder`, encodes rules, computes numer/denom weights (lines 162-206)\n23\t   - Uploads `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU (3 H2D copies)\n24\t   - Allocates `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `s_evals` output buffer\n25\t   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel via FFI\n26\t   - Returns `s_evals` DeviceBuffer\n27\t6. **SYNC**: `sum.to_host()` at `mod.rs:848` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n28\t7. CPU: Unzip frac, transpose, iDFT → `batch_sp_poly[2*i]`, `batch_sp_poly[2*i+1]`\n29\t\n30\t**Why this is slow with many AIRs:**\n31\t- 623 AIRs × 2 sync points = 1,246 GPU synchronizations via `cudaEventSynchronize`\n32\t- Each sync drains the GPU pipeline, preventing the next kernel from being submitted until the current one finishes AND the result is copied to host\n33\t- CPU work between syncs (DAG construction, iDFT, etc.) blocks kernel submission\n34\t- Per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` for intermediates adds runtime API overhead\n35\t- All work runs on `cudaStreamPerThread` (per-thread default stream), so operations are serialized\n36\t\n37\t**Profiling evidence (APC 300):**\n38\t- Total GPU kernel time in Round 0: ~490ms (measured via nsight kernel summary)\n39\t- Measured Round 0 wall time: 662ms\n40\t- Overhead (sync stalls, CPU work, alloc): ~172ms (26% of wall time)\n41\t- Key kernels: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel` (220ms, 539 instances), `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel` (195ms + 29ms, 735 instances)\n42\t\n43\t## Changes\n44\t\n45\t### Step 1: Extract interaction preparation from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n46\t\n47\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n48\t\n49\tCreate a new struct and function to pre-compute per-AIR interaction data:\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\tpub struct InteractionRound0Prep {\n53\t    pub rules: SymbolicRulesGpu,\n54\t    pub d_rules: DeviceBuffer<EncodedRule>,\n55\t    pub d_numer_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n56\t    pub d_denom_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n57\t    pub denom_sum_init: EF,\n58\t    pub buffer_size: u32,\n59\t}\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\tAdd function `prepare_round0_interactions(pk, symbolic, eq_3bs, beta_pows) -> Result<InteractionRound0Prep>` that extracts lines 161-212 from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. This performs:\n63\t- DAG construction via `SymbolicDagBuilder`\n64\t- Rule encoding\n65\t- Weight computation (numer, denom, denom_sum_init)\n66\t- H2D upload of rules and weights\n67\t\n68\t**Why**: Separates CPU-heavy preparation from kernel launch, allowing all preparation to be done upfront before any kernel launches.\n69\t\n70\t### Step 2: Create kernel-launch-only variants of the evaluation functions\n71\t\n72\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n73\t\n74\tAdd two new functions that take pre-allocated buffers and launch kernels without allocating or syncing:\n75\t\n76\t```rust\n77\tpub fn launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n78\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<...>,\n79\t    // ... same params as current evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu ...\n80\t    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n81\t    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n82\t    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n83\t) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\t```rust\n87\tpub fn launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n88\t    prep: &InteractionRound0Prep,\n89\t    // ... trace pointers, eq_cube, etc ...\n90\t    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n91\t    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n92\t    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n93\t) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\tThese functions call the same FFI (`zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`, `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`) but use externally-owned buffers instead of allocating their own. They do NOT perform D2H copies.\n97\t\n98\t**Why**: Decouples kernel launch from allocation and sync, enabling pipeline execution.\n99\t\n100\t### Step 3: Restructure the main loop in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n101\t\n102\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 720-884)\n103\t\n104\tReplace the single per-AIR loop with three phases:\n105\t\n106\t**Phase A — Prepare (CPU, before any kernel launches):**\n107\t```rust\n108\t// Pre-compute per-AIR metadata\n109\tlet mut per_air_data: Vec<Round0AirData> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n110\tfor (trace_idx, ...) in izip!(...).enumerate() {\n111\t    let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n112\t    let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n113\t    let local_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n114\t    let num_cosets_zc = local_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n115\t    let num_cosets_logup = local_deg;\n116\t    \n117\t    // Build interaction prep (currently done inside the loop at round0.rs:161-206)\n118\t    let interaction_prep = if !eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n119\t        Some(prepare_round0_interactions(single_pk, &symbolic, eq_3bs, &self.beta_pows)?)\n120\t    } else { None };\n121\t    \n122\t    // Compute main_parts, preprocessed_ptr\n123\t    let d_main_parts = ...;  // same as current lines 763-768\n124\t    \n125\t    per_air_data.push(Round0AirData {\n126\t        air_idx, n, height, local_deg, num_cosets_zc, num_cosets_logup,\n127\t        interaction_prep, d_main_parts, omega_root, eq_xi_ptr, ...\n128\t    });\n129\t}\n130\t\n131\t// Pre-allocate shared intermediate buffers (max size across all AIRs)\n132\tlet max_zc_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n133\tlet max_zc_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n134\tlet max_logup_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n135\tlet max_logup_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\n136\tlet mut zc_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermed.max(1));\n137\tlet mut zc_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp.max(1));\n138\tlet mut logup_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermed.max(1));\n139\tlet mut logup_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp.max(1));\n140\t\n141\t// Pre-allocate per-AIR output buffers\n142\tlet mut zc_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = per_air_data.iter()\n143\t    .map(|d| if d.num_cosets_zc > 0 { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_zc * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n144\t    .collect();\n145\tlet mut logup_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>> = per_air_data.iter()\n146\t    .map(|d| if d.has_interactions { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_logup * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n147\t    .collect();\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\t**Phase B — Launch all kernels (no sync):**\n151\t```rust\n152\tfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n153\t    // Launch zerocheck constraint kernel\n154\t    if data.num_cosets_zc > 0 {\n155\t        launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n156\t            &self.pk.per_air[data.air_idx], data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n157\t            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr, d_lambda_pows,\n158\t            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_zc,\n159\t            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n160\t            &mut zc_intermediates, &mut zc_temp_sums, &mut zc_outputs[trace_idx],\n161\t        )?;\n162\t    }\n163\t    // Launch logup interaction kernel\n164\t    if let Some(prep) = &data.interaction_prep {\n165\t        launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n166\t            prep, data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n167\t            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr,\n168\t            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_logup,\n169\t            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n170\t            &mut logup_intermediates, &mut logup_temp_sums, &mut logup_outputs[trace_idx],\n171\t        )?;\n172\t    }\n173\t}\n174\t// All kernels submitted. No to_host() calls above.\n175\t```\n176\t\n177\t**Phase C — Sync once + batch process results:**\n178\t```rust\n179\t// One sync (implicit in first to_host(), or explicit cudaDeviceSynchronize)\n180\tfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n181\t    // Process zerocheck output (same logic as current lines 791-826)\n182\t    if !zc_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n183\t        let q_evals = zc_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n184\t        // ... transpose, iDFT, compute sp_0 ...\n185\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx] = UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs);\n186\t    }\n187\t    // Process logup output (same logic as current lines 847-878)\n188\t    if !logup_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n189\t        let evals = logup_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n190\t        // ... unzip frac, transpose, iDFT ...\n191\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx] = numer_poly;\n192\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1] = denom_poly;\n193\t    }\n194\t}\n195\t```\n196\t\n197\t**Why**: The first `to_host()` in Phase C will synchronize the entire stream (all kernels are already done), and subsequent copies will execute instantly. The GPU pipeline is never stalled between kernel launches.\n198\t\n199\t### Step 4: Keep original functions as wrappers (backward compatibility)\n200\t\n201\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n202\t\n203\tKeep `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` as convenience wrappers that allocate, launch, and return. They remain available for any other callers but are no longer used by the hot path.\n204\t\n205\t**Why**: Minimizes risk. Other code paths that use these functions are unaffected.\n206\t\n207\t## Invariants\n208\t\n209\t1. **Correctness**: Each AIR produces the same polynomial evaluations as before. The kernel inputs are identical; only the timing of D2H copies changes.\n210\t2. **Intermediate buffer reuse**: On `cudaStreamPerThread`, kernels are serialized. The shared intermediate buffer is only accessed by one kernel at a time. Each kernel writes its output to a separate per-AIR DeviceBuffer.\n211\t3. **Memory safety**: Per-AIR output buffers are pre-allocated with the exact required capacity. Shared intermediate buffers are sized to the max across all AIRs. All buffers outlive the kernel launches (dropped after Phase C).\n212\t4. **Error handling**: If any kernel launch fails in Phase B, the error propagates immediately (before subsequent launches). CUDA runtime errors on the stream cause subsequent operations to fail, so partial failures are caught.\n213\t5. **Protocol unchanged**: The verifier is not modified. The same polynomials are produced; only the GPU execution order changes.\n214\t\n215\t## Measurement Plan\n216\t\n217\tRun the benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 (using `run_pairing.sh` in the powdr repo):\n218\t```bash\n219\tcd /home/georg/powdr && openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n220\t```\n221\t\n222\tAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare \"STARK (excl. trace)\" and its sub-components, particularly \"Round 0\":\n223\t```bash\n224\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\n225\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc100/metrics.json after_apc100\n226\tpython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n227\t```\n228\t\n229\t**Expected outcomes:**\n230\t- Round 0 at APC 300: from ~662ms to ~350-450ms (30-50% reduction)\n231\t- Round 0 at APC 0: roughly unchanged (few AIRs, sync overhead is small)\n232\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300: from ~2455ms to ~2150-2250ms (~10-15% reduction)\n233\t- No regression in correctness (prove+verify passes)\n234\t\n235\tAlso run nsight profiling for APC 300 to verify kernel pipelining:\n236\t```bash\n237\tnsys profile --output results/pairing/apc300/nsys_report --trace cuda,nvtx --sample none \\\n238\t  -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n239\t```\n240\t\n241\tLook for reduced gaps between kernel launches in the GPU timeline.\n242\t\n243\t## Rollback Criteria\n244\t\n245\t- Less than 10% improvement in Round 0 at APC 300 after full implementation\n246\t- Any correctness regression (prove fails or verify rejects)\n247\t- Peak GPU memory increases by more than 20% (unlikely given small output buffer overhead)\n248\t- Regression in APC 0 performance by more than 5%\n249\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fb0c9c1-c32f-45e4-afe7-f108d55d0327","uuid":"1fed47d3-341d-4deb-a40b-b03fb6ea68b1","timestamp":"2026-04-12T19:35:59.216Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pipeline Round 0 Kernel Launches\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR GPU synchronization in the Round 0 constraint evaluation loop to allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back without CPU stalls. This targets the largest sub-component regression in \"STARK excl. trace\": Round 0 increases from 178ms (APC 0, 99 AIRs) to 662ms (APC 300, 623 AIRs) despite a >2x reduction in total cells and constraints.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\nThe bottleneck is in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:598-884`.\n\n**Call chain (per AIR iteration, lines 732-880):**\n1. CPU: Prepare per-AIR data (constraints DAG, trace pointers, etc.)\n2. `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` at `round0.rs:31-124`:\n   - Allocates `intermediates` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n   - Allocates `temp_sums_buffer` (`DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`) — calls `cudaMallocAsync`\n   - Allocates `sp_evals` output buffer\n   - Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` kernel via FFI\n   - Returns `sp_evals` DeviceBuffer (intermediates and temp_sums dropped = `cudaFreeAsync`)\n3. **SYNC**: `sum_buffer.to_host()` at `mod.rs:792` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n4. CPU: Transpose, iDFT, polynomial construction → `batch_sp_poly[2*N + trace_idx]`\n5. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` at `round0.rs:132-275`:\n   - **CPU**: Builds `SymbolicDagBuilder`, encodes rules, computes numer/denom weights (lines 162-206)\n   - Uploads `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU (3 H2D copies)\n   - Allocates `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `s_evals` output buffer\n   - Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` kernel via FFI\n   - Returns `s_evals` DeviceBuffer\n6. **SYNC**: `sum.to_host()` at `mod.rs:848` — `cudaMemcpyAsync` + `cudaEventSynchronize`\n7. CPU: Unzip frac, transpose, iDFT → `batch_sp_poly[2*i]`, `batch_sp_poly[2*i+1]`\n\n**Why this is slow with many AIRs:**\n- 623 AIRs × 2 sync points = 1,246 GPU synchronizations via `cudaEventSynchronize`\n- Each sync drains the GPU pipeline, preventing the next kernel from being submitted until the current one finishes AND the result is copied to host\n- CPU work between syncs (DAG construction, iDFT, etc.) blocks kernel submission\n- Per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` for intermediates adds runtime API overhead\n- All work runs on `cudaStreamPerThread` (per-thread default stream), so operations are serialized\n\n**Profiling evidence (APC 300):**\n- Total GPU kernel time in Round 0: ~490ms (measured via nsight kernel summary)\n- Measured Round 0 wall time: 662ms\n- Overhead (sync stalls, CPU work, alloc): ~172ms (26% of wall time)\n- Key kernels: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel` (220ms, 539 instances), `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel` (195ms + 29ms, 735 instances)\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Extract interaction preparation from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nCreate a new struct and function to pre-compute per-AIR interaction data:\n\n```rust\npub struct InteractionRound0Prep {\n    pub rules: SymbolicRulesGpu,\n    pub d_rules: DeviceBuffer<EncodedRule>,\n    pub d_numer_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub d_denom_weights: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub denom_sum_init: EF,\n    pub buffer_size: u32,\n}\n```\n\nAdd function `prepare_round0_interactions(pk, symbolic, eq_3bs, beta_pows) -> Result<InteractionRound0Prep>` that extracts lines 161-212 from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. This performs:\n- DAG construction via `SymbolicDagBuilder`\n- Rule encoding\n- Weight computation (numer, denom, denom_sum_init)\n- H2D upload of rules and weights\n\n**Why**: Separates CPU-heavy preparation from kernel launch, allowing all preparation to be done upfront before any kernel launches.\n\n### Step 2: Create kernel-launch-only variants of the evaluation functions\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd two new functions that take pre-allocated buffers and launch kernels without allocating or syncing:\n\n```rust\npub fn launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<...>,\n    // ... same params as current evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu ...\n    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n```\n\n```rust\npub fn launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n    prep: &InteractionRound0Prep,\n    // ... trace pointers, eq_cube, etc ...\n    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n) -> Result<(), Round0EvalError>\n```\n\nThese functions call the same FFI (`zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`, `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0`) but use externally-owned buffers instead of allocating their own. They do NOT perform D2H copies.\n\n**Why**: Decouples kernel launch from allocation and sync, enabling pipeline execution.\n\n### Step 3: Restructure the main loop in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 720-884)\n\nReplace the single per-AIR loop with three phases:\n\n**Phase A — Prepare (CPU, before any kernel launches):**\n```rust\n// Pre-compute per-AIR metadata\nlet mut per_air_data: Vec<Round0AirData> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\nfor (trace_idx, ...) in izip!(...).enumerate() {\n    let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n    let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n    let local_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n    let num_cosets_zc = local_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n    let num_cosets_logup = local_deg;\n    \n    // Build interaction prep (currently done inside the loop at round0.rs:161-206)\n    let interaction_prep = if !eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n        Some(prepare_round0_interactions(single_pk, &symbolic, eq_3bs, &self.beta_pows)?)\n    } else { None };\n    \n    // Compute main_parts, preprocessed_ptr\n    let d_main_parts = ...;  // same as current lines 763-768\n    \n    per_air_data.push(Round0AirData {\n        air_idx, n, height, local_deg, num_cosets_zc, num_cosets_logup,\n        interaction_prep, d_main_parts, omega_root, eq_xi_ptr, ...\n    });\n}\n\n// Pre-allocate shared intermediate buffers (max size across all AIRs)\nlet max_zc_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet max_zc_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| zc_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet max_logup_intermed = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_intermediates_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet max_logup_temp = per_air_data.iter().map(|d| logup_temp_size(d)).max().unwrap_or(0);\nlet mut zc_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermed.max(1));\nlet mut zc_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp.max(1));\nlet mut logup_intermediates = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermed.max(1));\nlet mut logup_temp_sums = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp.max(1));\n\n// Pre-allocate per-AIR output buffers\nlet mut zc_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>> = per_air_data.iter()\n    .map(|d| if d.num_cosets_zc > 0 { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_zc * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n    .collect();\nlet mut logup_outputs: Vec<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>> = per_air_data.iter()\n    .map(|d| if d.has_interactions { DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(d.num_cosets_logup * skip_domain) } else { DeviceBuffer::new() })\n    .collect();\n```\n\n**Phase B — Launch all kernels (no sync):**\n```rust\nfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n    // Launch zerocheck constraint kernel\n    if data.num_cosets_zc > 0 {\n        launch_round0_constraints_kernel(\n            &self.pk.per_air[data.air_idx], data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr, d_lambda_pows,\n            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_zc,\n            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n            &mut zc_intermediates, &mut zc_temp_sums, &mut zc_outputs[trace_idx],\n        )?;\n    }\n    // Launch logup interaction kernel\n    if let Some(prep) = &data.interaction_prep {\n        launch_round0_interactions_kernel(\n            prep, data.selectors, &data.d_main_parts,\n            data.public_values, data.eq_xi_ptr,\n            skip_domain, data.num_x, data.height, data.num_cosets_logup,\n            data.omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n            &mut logup_intermediates, &mut logup_temp_sums, &mut logup_outputs[trace_idx],\n        )?;\n    }\n}\n// All kernels submitted. No to_host() calls above.\n```\n\n**Phase C — Sync once + batch process results:**\n```rust\n// One sync (implicit in first to_host(), or explicit cudaDeviceSynchronize)\nfor (trace_idx, data) in per_air_data.iter().enumerate() {\n    // Process zerocheck output (same logic as current lines 791-826)\n    if !zc_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n        let q_evals = zc_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n        // ... transpose, iDFT, compute sp_0 ...\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx] = UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs);\n    }\n    // Process logup output (same logic as current lines 847-878)\n    if !logup_outputs[trace_idx].is_empty() {\n        let evals = logup_outputs[trace_idx].to_host()?;\n        // ... unzip frac, transpose, iDFT ...\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx] = numer_poly;\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1] = denom_poly;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Why**: The first `to_host()` in Phase C will synchronize the entire stream (all kernels are already done), and subsequent copies will execute instantly. The GPU pipeline is never stalled between kernel launches.\n\n### Step 4: Keep original functions as wrappers (backward compatibility)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nKeep `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` as convenience wrappers that allocate, launch, and return. They remain available for any other callers but are no longer used by the hot path.\n\n**Why**: Minimizes risk. Other code paths that use these functions are unaffected.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Each AIR produces the same polynomial evaluations as before. The kernel inputs are identical; only the timing of D2H copies changes.\n2. **Intermediate buffer reuse**: On `cudaStreamPerThread`, kernels are serialized. The shared intermediate buffer is only accessed by one kernel at a time. Each kernel writes its output to a separate per-AIR DeviceBuffer.\n3. **Memory safety**: Per-AIR output buffers are pre-allocated with the exact required capacity. Shared intermediate buffers are sized to the max across all AIRs. All buffers outlive the kernel launches (dropped after Phase C).\n4. **Error handling**: If any kernel launch fails in Phase B, the error propagates immediately (before subsequent launches). CUDA runtime errors on the stream cause subsequent operations to fail, so partial failures are caught.\n5. **Protocol unchanged**: The verifier is not modified. The same polynomials are produced; only the GPU execution order changes.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\nRun the benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 (using `run_pairing.sh` in the powdr repo):\n```bash\ncd /home/georg/powdr && openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n```\n\nAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare \"STARK (excl. trace)\" and its sub-components, particularly \"Round 0\":\n```bash\npython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc000/metrics.json after_apc000\npython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc100/metrics.json after_apc100\npython3 /home/georg/spec.py results/pairing/apc300/metrics.json after_apc300\n```\n\n**Expected outcomes:**\n- Round 0 at APC 300: from ~662ms to ~350-450ms (30-50% reduction)\n- Round 0 at APC 0: roughly unchanged (few AIRs, sync overhead is small)\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300: from ~2455ms to ~2150-2250ms (~10-15% reduction)\n- No regression in correctness (prove+verify passes)\n\nAlso run nsight profiling for APC 300 to verify kernel pipelining:\n```bash\nnsys profile --output results/pairing/apc300/nsys_report --trace cuda,nvtx --sample none \\\n  -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n```\n\nLook for reduced gaps between kernel launches in the GPU timeline.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Less than 10% improvement in Round 0 at APC 300 after full implementation\n- Any correctness regression (prove fails or verify rejects)\n- Peak GPU memory increases by more than 20% (unlikely given small output buffer overhead)\n- Regression in APC 0 performance by more than 5%\n","numLines":249,"startLine":1,"totalLines":249}}}
