{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6G2gkUYckj5PWZe31TDJ9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-12-2130-pipeline-round0-kernel-launches\n2\t\n3\tThe Round 0 constraint evaluation loop in `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` processes each AIR instance sequentially with two GPU sync points per AIR (`to_host()` at lines 792 and 848). With 623 AIR instances at APC 300, this creates 1,246 GPU synchronizations that serialize the pipeline and prevent the GPU from keeping its execution queue full. Eliminating these per-AIR sync points by deferring all D2H copies to after all kernel launches will allow the GPU to execute kernels back-to-back, reducing Round 0 from ~662ms to an estimated ~300-400ms at APC 300.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYMF7fsT7WkEvXM5zyVC4P","session_id":"9fb0c9c1-c32f-45e4-afe7-f108d55d0327","uuid":"6084a779-b9d5-426e-ada3-3a74cbcd0a57","timestamp":"2026-04-12T19:37:43.379Z"}
